# Security Review Protocol — Backend, Auth & Telemetry

Applies to offline-first sync, HTTP adapters (Fase 7), JWT auth, score payloads, and local persistence for the LOTO training simulation.

**Trigger:** Any PR or agent task modifying paths in `globs` above → run `/review-security` before merge.

**Automated gate:** `python tools/ci/validate_security_surface.py` in CI on matching path changes.

---

## Severity model

| Level | Meaning | Merge policy |
|-------|---------|--------------|
| `[CRITICAL]` | Credential leak, score tampering vector, data loss, auth bypass | Block merge |
| `[HIGH]` | Missing timeout, race condition with data corruption risk, PII exposure | Fix before merge |
| `[MEDIUM]` | Weak logging hygiene, missing retry bounds, incomplete validation | Fix or documented accept |
| `[INFO]` | Hardening suggestion, defense-in-depth | Optional |

Report format per finding:

```
[SEVERITY] Title
Location: path:line
Vector: <category>
Finding: <what is wrong>
Mitigation: <specific fix>
```

---

## Inspection vectors (mandatory)

### V1 — Credentials & tokens

- [ ] No JWT, API keys, passwords, or serial numbers in source, comments, or committed config
- [ ] No `Debug.Log` / `Debug.LogWarning` printing tokens, headers, or full request bodies
- [ ] Tokens not stored in `PlayerPrefs` without encryption and expiry handling
- [ ] Auth headers set only in adapter layer — not duplicated across managers
- [ ] VR login: username/token field only — no password entry in headset (RNF08, VR-APP-01)
- [ ] JWT expiry respected (2h VR per RNF08) — reject expired tokens before session start

### V2 — Score payload integrity

- [ ] `SimulationResultPayload` built only via `LotoSessionScore.Build()` — no client-side score override after build
- [ ] Objective weights read from `LotoObjectiveIds.GetWeightPercent` — not hardcoded in adapter
- [ ] `scoreTotal` clamped 0–100; `approved` derived from threshold (60%), not set independently
- [ ] `sessionId` on payload matches active `SimulationSessionContext` — no session swapping
- [ ] Event records (`SimulationEventRecord`) append-only during session — no retroactive tampering
- [ ] False-positive penalty applied in `LotoSessionScore.ComputePartial` — not skippable via adapter

### V3 — Local persistence & PII

- [ ] Files under `Application.persistentDataPath` only — no `StreamingAssets` writes for scores
- [ ] No PII beyond `participantId` / `sessionId` in DTOs or JSON files
- [ ] `ScorePersistantData.json` never deleted on sync failure
- [ ] Queue file (`PendingSyncQueue.json`) writable only through `SyncQueueManager` — no parallel writers

### V4 — Sync queue resilience

- [ ] Queue NOT flushed when `ISimulationBackendAdapter.IsAvailable` is false
- [ ] 24h purge (`SyncRetentionHours`) — stale entries removed, not retried indefinitely
- [ ] `retryCount` increments on failure; `lastError` populated; no silent drop
- [ ] Partial flush: synced entries removed, failed entries retained (WF3 F4)
- [ ] No race: concurrent `TryFlushQueueAsync` calls do not corrupt `queueData` or double-send
- [ ] `Enqueue` + `SaveQueue` atomic — file not left half-written on crash (best-effort verify)

### V5 — Network & HTTP (Fase 7)

- [ ] HTTPS only (`https://`) — no cleartext endpoints (RNF06 TLS 1.2+)
- [ ] Request timeout configured (recommend ≤10s; gameplay never blocks on await)
- [ ] Adapter returns `false` on timeout/4xx/5xx — entry stays in queue
- [ ] No gameplay `await` on network — fire-and-forget or background Task
- [ ] `IBManager.SendScoreToCloud` and `/crearSimReporte` unchanged unless explicitly approved

### V6 — Serialization safety

- [ ] `JsonUtility` wrapper classes for lists — no raw array serialization bugs
- [ ] `payloadJson` in `PendingSyncEntry` round-trips without data loss
- [ ] Deserialization failures handled — corrupt entry quarantined, not crash loop

